    "DIAGNOSIS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS",
          "canonical_heading": "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Freckles (nevi) on the surface of the iris that do not appear to change over time—may be benign pigmented lesions; more likely melanocytoma, a benign lesion.",
              "pdf_page": 1470,
              "printed_page": 1388,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Heterochromia irides—congenital, nonprogressive alteration in iridal pigmentation.",
              "pdf_page": 1470,
              "printed_page": 1388,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Diffuse iridal color change that results from chronic anterior uveitis. Differs from uveal melanoma by the history of chronic anterior uveitis.",
              "pdf_page": 1470,
              "printed_page": 1388,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Iris atrophy—the anterior iris stroma is lost, increasing visualization of the heavily pigmented posterior iris tissue. Iris thinning is seen as fullthickness holes in the iris or as retroillumination defects in the iris when light is bounced off the tapetum back through the iris.",
              "pdf_page": 1470,
              "printed_page": 1388,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Limbal melanomas—benign behavior; usually focal, superiorly located, flat to slightly",
              "pdf_page": 1470,
              "printed_page": 1388,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "raised limbal masses that do not invade the uveal tract unless they are very large.",
              "pdf_page": 1470,
              "printed_page": 1388,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
